From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:45:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: leave the PlatformRequestHandler system limit update
 to runtime

_pfmreqhndlrCallPshareStatus() handled a pending system parameter limit update
during init too, before PSHAREPARAMS has set up the TGPU and PPMD counters, so
both limit queries failed with NV_ERR_INVALID_DATA at every boot ("failed to
get target temp from SBIOS", "failed to get platform power mode from SBIOS").
Every other update in that function is either init-only or skipped at init;
skip this one at init as well. PSHAREPARAMS samples the initial PPMD limit
itself, and the TGPU limit counter is sampled on request.

Fixes upstream issue 1360.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/kernel/platform/platform_request_handler_ctrl.c   | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/platform_request_handler_ctrl.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/platform_request_handler_ctrl.c
index 803f3d1b..17eba1eb 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/platform_request_handler_ctrl.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/platform_request_handler_ctrl.c
@@ -2477,7 +2477,13 @@ _pfmreqhndlrCallPshareStatus
             }
         }
 
-        if (pPfmreqhndlrData->PFMREQHNDLRACPIData.bSystemParamLimitUpdate)
+        //
+        // 4. System parameter limit update. At init, the TGPU and PPMD
+        // counters aren't set up before PSHAREPARAMS has been called, which
+        // also samples the initial PPMD limit. Like the other updates, leave
+        // it to the runtime PSHARESTATUS calls.
+        //
+        if (pPfmreqhndlrData->PFMREQHNDLRACPIData.bSystemParamLimitUpdate && !bInit)
         {
             timeStamp = _pfmreqhndlrGetTimeStamp(pPlatformRequestHandler);
             _pfmreqhndlrResetCounter(pPfmreqhndlrData, PFM_REQ_HNDLR_LIMIT(PFM_REQ_HNDLR_TGPU_SENSOR), timeStamp);
